IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XX -- OFFENCES AND PUNISHMENT (ss 250 to 252).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes anyone's point of view.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE READS THE TEXT.
--   * "Guilty of an offence" is a decision: the elements of the offence, less the defences the Act itself
--     states. Whether the facts are proved is for the court and is the caller's input.
--   * Punishment is a ceiling (see cb5-nouns.l4), never a sentence. Where the Act states none, the answer
--     is NOTHING: the Act does not say, and no figure is invented.
--   * Time is counted by the keel's convention (fork F1 in the keel's notes).

§ `Part XX -- Offences and punishment`

§§ `s 250 -- offences with respect to reports`

-- (4) comes first because (1) depends on it: the Act's register of individuals with significant control is
-- not a "report, return, notice or other document" for the purposes of s 250.
-- src:3124 | (4) For greater certainty, a register referred to in subsection 21.1(1) or an extract from it is not a report, return, notice or other document for the purposes of this section.
@ref CBCA s 250(4) (src:3124)
GIVEN `the document is a report, return, notice or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a register referred to in subsection 21.1(1) or an extract from it` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 21.1 (piece cb1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document is a report, return, notice or other document for the purposes of s 250 within s 250(4)` IF
        `the document is a report, return, notice or other document`
    AND (NOT `the document is a register referred to in subsection 21.1(1) or an extract from it`)

-- The offender "makes or assists in making" the document; the document is "required by this Act or the
-- regulations to be sent to the Director or to any other person"; and (a) it contains an untrue statement
-- of a material fact OR (b) it omits to state a material fact (required, or necessary to make a statement not
-- misleading). The elements only: the immunity of subsection (3) is a separate rule below.
-- src:3115 | 250 (1) A person who makes or assists in making a report, return, notice or other document required by this Act or the regulations to be sent to the Director or to any other person that
-- src:3116 | (a) contains an untrue statement of a material fact, or
-- src:3117 | (b) omits to state a material fact required therein or necessary to make a statement contained therein not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made
-- src:3118 | is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 250(1) (src:3115-3118)
GIVEN `the person makes or assists in making the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is required by this Act or the regulations to be sent to the Director or to any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a report, return, notice or other document for the purposes of s 250` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document contains an untrue statement of a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document omits to state a material fact required in it or necessary to make a statement contained in it not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the elements of the offence are met within s 250(1)` IF
        `the person makes or assists in making the document`
    AND `the document is required by this Act or the regulations to be sent to the Director or to any other person`
    AND `the document is a report, return, notice or other document for the purposes of s 250`
    AND (    `the document contains an untrue statement of a material fact`
         OR  `the document omits to state a material fact required in it or necessary to make a statement contained in it not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made`)

-- (3): the defence. "Did not know, and in the exercise of reasonable diligence could not have known": both
-- limbs, joined by "and".
-- src:3122 | (3) No person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2) if the person did not know, and in the exercise of reasonable diligence could not have known, of the untrue statement or omission.
@ref CBCA s 250(3) (src:3122)
GIVEN `the person did not know of the untrue statement or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the exercise of reasonable diligence the person could not have known of the untrue statement or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has the immunity within s 250(3)` IF
        `the person did not know of the untrue statement or omission`
    AND `in the exercise of reasonable diligence the person could not have known of the untrue statement or omission`

-- src:3115 | 250 (1) A person who makes or assists in making a report, return, notice or other document required by this Act or the regulations to be sent to the Director or to any other person that
-- src:3116 | (a) contains an untrue statement of a material fact, or
-- src:3117 | (b) omits to state a material fact required therein or necessary to make a statement contained therein not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made
-- src:3118 | is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
-- src:3122 | (3) No person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2) if the person did not know, and in the exercise of reasonable diligence could not have known, of the untrue statement or omission.
@ref CBCA s 250(1) (src:3115-3118 src:3122)
GIVEN `the elements of the offence are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the immunity of subsection 250(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of an offence within s 250(1) and s 250(3)` IF
        `the elements of the offence are met`
    AND (NOT `the person has the immunity of subsection 250(3)`)

-- src:3118 | is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 250(1) (src:3118)
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment on summary conviction`
`the most the court may impose within s 250(1)` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment on summary conviction` WITH
        `largest fine in dollars` IS 5_000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS 6
        `fine and imprisonment may both be imposed` IS TRUE

-- (2): the body corporate commits an offence under (1); a director or officer who knowingly authorized,
-- permitted or acquiesced is a party to it and guilty, "whether or not the body corporate has been
-- prosecuted or convicted", so no input about the body corporate's prosecution is taken. (3) applies to
-- "any person", so the director's own immunity is taken too.
-- src:3120 | (2) Where a body corporate commits an offence under subsection (1), any director or officer of the body corporate who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both, whether or not the body corporate has been prosecuted or convicted.
-- src:3122 | (3) No person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2) if the person did not know, and in the exercise of reasonable diligence could not have known, of the untrue statement or omission.
@ref CBCA s 250(2) (src:3120 src:3122)
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 250(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the immunity of subsection 250(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director or officer is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 250(2)` IF
        `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 250(1)`
    AND `the person is a director or officer of the body corporate`
    AND `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence`
    AND (NOT `the person has the immunity of subsection 250(3)`)

-- src:3120 | (2) Where a body corporate commits an offence under subsection (1), any director or officer of the body corporate who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both, whether or not the body corporate has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref CBCA s 250(2) (src:3120)
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment on summary conviction`
`the most the court may impose on a director or officer within s 250(2)` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment on summary conviction` WITH
        `largest fine in dollars` IS 5_000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS 6
        `fine and imprisonment may both be imposed` IS TRUE

§§ `s 251 -- the general offence`

-- Three elements: a contravention of a provision of the Act or the regulations; no punishment provided for
-- that provision; no reasonable cause. The punishment is "punishable on summary conviction" and the text
-- states no maximum, so the answer below is NOTHING (the default for summary convictions lies in another
-- Act, which is not among the sources).
-- src:3126 | 251 Every person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes a provision of this Act or the regulations for which no punishment is provided is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref CBCA s 251 (src:3126)
GIVEN `the person contravenes a provision of this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no punishment is provided for the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of an offence within s 251` IF
        `the person contravenes a provision of this Act or the regulations`
    AND `no punishment is provided for the provision`
    AND (NOT `the person had reasonable cause`)

-- src:3126 | 251 Every person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes a provision of this Act or the regulations for which no punishment is provided is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref CBCA s 251 (src:3126)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum punishment on summary conviction`
`the most the court may impose within s 251` MEANS NOTHING

§§ `s 252 -- order to comply, limitation, civil remedies`

-- Three things must be true: the person is guilty of an offence under the Act or the regulations; the
-- person has been convicted of the contravention; and the court is one "in which proceedings in respect of
-- the offence are taken". The order is "in addition to any punishment".
-- src:3128 | 252 (1) Where a person is guilty of an offence under this Act or the regulations, any court in which proceedings in respect of the offence are taken may, in addition to any punishment it may impose, order that person to comply with the provisions of this Act or the regulations for the contravention of which the person has been convicted.
@ref CBCA s 252(1) (src:3128)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been convicted of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings in respect of the offence are taken in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order the person to comply within s 252(1)` IF
        `the person is guilty of an offence under this Act or the regulations`
    AND `the person has been convicted of the contravention`
    AND `proceedings in respect of the offence are taken in the court`

-- Two years, counted from "the time when the subject-matter of the complaint arose".
-- src:3130 | (2) A prosecution for an offence under this Act may be instituted at any time within but not later than two years after the time when the subject-matter of the complaint arose.
@ref CBCA s 252(2) (src:3130)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the period for instituting a prosecution within s 252(2)` MEANS
    `Time limit` WITH
        `number of units` IS 2
        `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:3130 | (2) A prosecution for an offence under this Act may be instituted at any time within but not later than two years after the time when the subject-matter of the complaint arose.
@ref CBCA s 252(2) (src:3130)
GIVEN `the date the subject-matter of the complaint arose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day to institute a prosecution within s 252(2)` IS
    `the last day of` `the period for instituting a prosecution within s 252(2)` `counted from` `the date the subject-matter of the complaint arose`

-- src:3130 | (2) A prosecution for an offence under this Act may be instituted at any time within but not later than two years after the time when the subject-matter of the complaint arose.
@ref CBCA s 252(2) (src:3130)
GIVEN `the date the subject-matter of the complaint arose` IS A DATE
      `the date the prosecution is instituted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prosecution is instituted in time within s 252(2)` IF
    `done within the time limit` `the period for instituting a prosecution within s 252(2)` `the date the subject-matter of the complaint arose` `the date the prosecution is instituted`

-- src:3132 | (3) No civil remedy for an act or omission is suspended or affected by reason that the act or omission is an offence under this Act.
@ref CBCA s 252(3) (src:3132)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a civil remedy is suspended or affected by reason that the act or omission is an offence under this Act within s 252(3)` MEANS FALSE
